Z||000003||007DOUG||09-07-2000||11:42 PM||||I'd vote NO, considering I've got ALL parts needed to convert the rear/side of your fiero to a fastback GT for $600. Including new GT windows and side AERO mouldings.<P>------------------<BR>4 Indy pace Cars<BR>84 T-top<BR>84 SE<BR>86 SE V6 153K<BR>2 86 GT's<BR>86 GT 3.4 Pearl White T-top<BR>2 88 GT twins<P>However......<BR><I>"Time is my most precious and most perishable of all my possessions."</I>||||reg||13
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||09-08-2000||12:25 AM||||If the tail lights, sail windows, deck lid, rear wiring harness, trunk hardware (little half moon pieces, gasket and a couple other brackets), deck vents and brackets are all there and undamaged that is a good price. If there are parts missing or broken (namely tail lights or sail windows) then it could cost you another chunk of change for those things. <P>I got pretty lucky. I got a clip with great paint, and the same color as my car, with good windows and tail lights for helping a friend switch motors in his Fiero.||||reg||1
